### Note: This file is used to test and validate the Client Management Endpoints.
### It aligns perfectly with the ClientsController routes and MediatR commands.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5165/api
@contentType = application/json

### 1. Register a New Client
### Creates a new client user profile in the system with a unique library card.
POST {{baseUrl}}/Clients
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "Mohammad@gmail.com",
  "password": "Mohammad1234#",
  "firstName": "Mohammad",
  "lastName": "Atieh",
  "phoneNumber": "0780830732",
  "address": "Al-Zarqa",
  "userName": "Mohammad",
  "countryId": 113,
  "birthDate": "1973-10-06",
  "imageUrl": "",
  "libraryCardNumber": "230221"
}

### ------------------------------------------------------------------

### 2. Get Paginated Clients List
### Retrieves all active clients using query string routing parameters.
GET {{baseUrl}}/Clients?pageNumber=1&pageSize=10
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

### ------------------------------------------------------------------

### 3. Get Authenticated Client Profile
### Automatically parses identity token claims from incoming HTTP request context/cookies.
GET {{baseUrl}}/Clients/get-client-profile/2
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

### ------------------------------------------------------------------

### 4. Update Client Information
### Updates demographic and account info. Route ID must match the body payload ClientId.
PUT {{baseUrl}}/Clients/update-client-info/2
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "clientId": 2,
  "libraryCardNumber": "230220"
}

### ------------------------------------------------------------------

### 5. Delete Client Profile (Soft Delete)
### Flags the target client entity as deleted using the unique user primary key tracking identifier.
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/Clients/delete-client/2/user/8
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

### ------------------------------------------------------------------

### 6. Restore Soft-Deleted Client
### Reverses the soft delete state to re-enable database inclusion and portal access.
### Note: Route reflects the exact variable configuration string definition ('resotre-client').
PUT {{baseUrl}}/Clients/resotre-client/2/user/8
Content-Type: {{contentType}}